cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  paint-by-words: goal-conditioned intervention retrieval from a Cell Painting archive
message: If you use this software or its evaluation protocol, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Le
    given-names: Nam H.
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6862-9257
    affiliation: Department of Computer Science, University of Vermont
    email: nam.le@uvm.edu
repository-code: https://github.com/drnamlabs-gif/paint-by-words
url: https://drnamlabs.com
abstract: >-
  Ask a cell-image archive for a phenotype in plain English and get a compound, a dose
  and the evidence, or a refusal. Built on RxRx3-core. Includes the measurement finding
  that per-cell CellProfiler features, being averaged over segmented survivors, are
  entangled with cell death strongly enough that a baseline which never reads the
  request accounts for almost all of the apparent accuracy, together with the one-line
  control that detects it and the redefinition that removes it.
keywords:
  - Cell Painting
  - high-content screening
  - phenotypic drug discovery
  - language-conditioned control
  - evaluation
  - trivial baselines
  - selective prediction
  - dose response
license: MIT
